.*
.* QUIDSPUDFS: DSPUDFS, one user-defined file system and the directories
.* it is mounted over. No oracle has a UDFS (pub400 answers CPFA0A9,
.* golden/audit/displays/dspudfs-none), so the layout follows IBM's
.* documentation.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=PATHCL BASETYPE='CHAR 44'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=STAMPCL BASETYPE='CHAR 18'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TEXTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 50'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=MNTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 76'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=UDFS CLASS=PATHCL.
:VAR NAME=OWNER CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=CASE CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=DFTFMT CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=CRTAUD CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=CRTDTS CLASS=STAMPCL.
:VAR NAME=MOUNTED CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=TEXT CLASS=TEXTCL.
:VAR NAME=MNTDIR CLASS=MNTCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=MOUNTS VARS='MNTDIR'.
:KEYL NAME=DSPKEYS HELP=KEYSHLP.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=DSPUDFS KEYL=DSPKEYS HELP=DSPUDFS ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Display User-Defined FS
:DATA DEPTH=10.
:DATACOL WIDTH=32.
:DATACOL WIDTH=78.
:DATAI VAR=UDFS USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/UDFS'.User-defined file system
:DATAI VAR=OWNER USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/OWNER'.Owner
:DATAI VAR=CASE USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/CASE'.Case sensitivity
:DATAI VAR=DFTFMT USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/DFTFMT'.Default file format
:DATAI VAR=CRTAUD USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/CRTAUD'.Create object auditing value
:DATAI VAR=CRTDTS USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/CRTDTS'.Creation date/time
:DATAI VAR=TEXT USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/TEXT'.Text description
:DATAC.
:DATAI VAR=MOUNTED USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/MOUNTED'.Mounted
:EDATA.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=MOUNTS SCROLL=YES.(Not mounted)
:LISTCOL VAR=MNTDIR USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/MNTDIR'.Mounted over
:ELIST.
:BOTINST.Press Enter to continue.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=DSPUDFS.Display User-Defined FS - Help
:P.A user-defined file system: who owns it, whether its names are case
sensitive, the auditing value its new objects get, when it was created,
and the directories it is mounted over now.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=KEYSHLP.Function keys - Help
:P.F3 and F12 leave.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='FLD/UDFS'.User-defined file system
:P.The user-defined file system shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OWNER'.Owner
:P.The owner of the objects created.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CASE'.Case sensitivity
:P.The case sensitivity shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/DFTFMT'.Default file format
:P.The default file format shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CRTAUD'.Create object auditing value
:P.The create object auditing value shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CRTDTS'.Creation date/time
:P.The creation date/time shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/TEXT'.Text description
:P.The text description shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/MOUNTED'.Mounted
:P.The mounted shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/MNTDIR'.Mounted over
:P.The mounted over of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
